<p>The venue was further highlighted in the 1884 Mandan Pioneer Immigrant Edition, touting the cultural and social activities associated with a city of 2500 only three years in existance. The original east end stage was described as "large enough for all ordinary purposes," being provided with scenergy, foot-lights and all the accessories necessary for a "first class proscenium." Tuttle and Wilson were the original facility managers; but by 1884 H.R. Lyon had assumed the role as manager. Click to Open 1884 Newspaper Description</p>

