<p>Opera House circa 1906 The venue was listed in national theatrical guides as originally having a 30' x 40' stage, with a proscenium with 20 wide feet and height of 12 feet. It had seating for 300 (with chair rental available through Binginheimer &amp; Taylor's Drug Store) and piano and scenery was available on-site. The building was a civic highlight of the Souvenir Book published in 1906 to promote the City of Mandan and the economic opportunities available here.</p>

<p>Events included 4th of July and New Year's Eve dances plus live performances which ranged from serious drama to vaudeville acts. Basketball games, graduation ceremonies and public meetings were also held at the site. A major addition to the east side of the building was completed in the Spring of 1893, expanding the stage and backstage areas and increasing seating to 500. The facility was renamed the Opera House with the completion of the addition.</p>

